#~
A minor collection leaves an Int alone, whatever its value (#1452).

The collector relocated every operand-stack word that looked like a young
object: when an object moved, any word equal to its old address was rewritten
to the new one. An Int is not a reference, but one can equal an address:
GetInstanceID() returns the object's. Run() keeps such an Int pending on the
stack while Churn() allocates enough to collect, and compares it with the same
value kept in a typed Int local, which the collector never touched. With a
64k nursery about one comparison in eight came back changed.

The collector now asks the operand stack's reference maps which words are
references (docs/GC_ROOTS_DESIGN.md, phase 2). The regression runner cannot
pass VM flags, and with the default nursery no collection lands in the
window, so here the test is vacuous. run_vm_flag_tests.py (section 25) runs
it with --nursery=64k, interpreted.

This test no longer has a trigger. Instance IDs are counters now, not
addresses (#1472), so Objeck code can no longer produce an Int equal to an
object's address: the old guess has nothing here to rewrite either. The test
guards against a regression in how IDs are kept, and does not show that the
reference maps type the stack correctly. The negative control that expected
a failure under the old guess (OBJECK_GC_ROOTS=conservative) was removed for
that reason; #1473 plans a test-only way to make such an Int, which phase 3's
compiled configurations need too.
~#

class Box {
  @v : Int;

  New(v : Int) {
    @v := v;
  }

  method : public : Get() ~ Int {
    return @v;
  }
}

class GcIntNotRelocated {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    bad := Run();
    if(bad = 0) {
      "PASS: no pending Int was rewritten by a collection"->PrintLine();
    }
    else {
      "FAIL: {$bad} pending Int value(s) changed by a collection"->PrintLine();
      Runtime->Exit(1);
    };
  }

  function : Run() ~ Int {
    bad := 0;
    for(i := 0; i < 2000; i += 1;) {
      o := Box->New(i);
      before := o->GetInstanceID();
      # the id is pending on the operand stack while Churn allocates
      if(Same(o->GetInstanceID(), Churn(i), before) = false) {
        bad += 1;
      };
    };
    return bad;
  }

  function : Same(a : Int, c : Int, b : Int) ~ Bool {
    return a = b;
  }

  function : Churn(n : Int) ~ Int {
    s := 0;
    for(j := 0; j < 200; j += 1;) {
      b := Box->New(j);
      s += b->Get();
    };
    return s;
  }
}
